<Description>
    <Header>
        <h1 id="contribution-guide" class="cg-toc-anchor">Contribution Guide</h1>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Thank you for your interest in contributing to the <strong>Syncfusion<sup style="font-size:70%">&reg;</sup> Toolkit for Blazor</strong>. This guide is for both <strong>human contributors</strong> and <strong>AI coding agents</strong>: every step is described concretely enough that you can follow it end-to-end without additional research or guesswork.</p>
        <p>If you are planning a bigger change &mdash; a new component, a breaking API change, a large refactor &mdash; please open an issue or talk to a core team member first. We will help you confirm the change is in scope, that it can be reviewed promptly, and that you do not invest time in something we cannot accept.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="code-of-conduct" class="cg-toc-anchor">Code of Conduct</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>By participating in this project you agree to follow the <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Syncfusion Code of Conduct and Corporate Ethics Policy</a>. It aligns with the community standards of open-source initiatives maintained by Syncfusion, including the Syncfusion Blazor Toolkit.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="ways-to-contribute" class="cg-toc-anchor">Ways to contribute</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>You do not have to write C# to help. Some of the most valuable contributions are smaller than a full PR:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Bug fixes</strong> &mdash; anything tagged <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22t%2Fbug%22" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>t/bug</code></a> in the issue tracker.</li>
            <li><strong>Documentation</strong> &mdash; typo fixes, new examples, missing API descriptions, accessibility notes. The samples browser source lives under <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/samples/Blazor.Toolkit.Samples.Client" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>samples/Blazor.Toolkit.Samples.Client</code></a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Tests</strong> &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">bUnit</a> and <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Playwright.Test" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Playwright</a> regression tests. <span class="cg-tag">Especially welcome</span></li>
            <li><strong>Accessibility</strong> &mdash; keyboard navigation, ARIA, focus management, contrast. See <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/accessibility" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/accessibility/</code></a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Performance</strong> &mdash; render-path profiling, allocation reductions. The <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/evidences/performance" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">performance evidence</a> under <code>.github/evidences/performance/</code> captures the latest profiling notes.</li>
            <li><strong>Feature proposals</strong> &mdash; new components, new parameters on existing components, new CSS hooks. See <a href="#proposing-larger-features">Proposing larger features</a> below.</li>
            <li><strong>Issue triage</strong> &mdash; reproduction, labelling, and confirming duplicate reports.</li>
        </ul>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="finding-something-to-work-on" class="cg-toc-anchor">Finding something to work on</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Good starting points, in order of recommendation for first-time contributors:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Issues labelled <code>good first issue</code></a> &mdash; small, well-scoped, and explicitly tagged as friendly to first-timers.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22help+wanted%22" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Issues labelled <code>help wanted</code></a> &mdash; community contributions are particularly welcome.</li>
            <li>The <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+milestone%3ABacklog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Backlog milestone</a> &mdash; any unassigned item is up for grabs. Open the issue, leave a comment saying you would like to take it, and start work.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="cg-callout">
            <strong>Before you start:</strong> open or claim an issue so the team knows you are working on it. Two people picking up the same issue wastes effort.
        </div>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="prerequisites" class="cg-toc-anchor">Prerequisites &amp; development environment</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>The toolkit builds and runs on <strong>Windows</strong>, <strong>Linux</strong>, and <strong>macOS</strong>. Either an IDE or the <code>dotnet</code> CLI works.</p>

        <h3>Tools you need</h3>
        <table class="cg-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Tool</th>
                    <th>Version</th>
                    <th>Notes</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">.NET SDK</a></td>
                    <td>8.0, 9.0, or 10.0</td>
                    <td>CI builds and tests all three; pick the highest available.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/downloads/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Visual Studio 2022</a> (Windows) <em>or</em> <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/download" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">VS Code</a> (cross-platform) <em>or</em> <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/rider/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">JetBrains Rider</a></td>
                    <td>Latest stable</td>
                    <td>Any modern C# IDE works. VS Code needs the C# Dev Kit extension.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Node.js (LTS) + npm</td>
                    <td>Node 22 (CI uses 22)</td>
                    <td>CI runs the ESLint security scan (<code>npm run lint:security</code>) and the XSS / unsafe markup scan (<code>npx gulp security-xss-scan</code>). Install dependencies with <code>npm ci</code> before opening a PR.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Git</td>
                    <td>2.30+</td>
                    <td>For working with branches and PRs.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3>Clone the repository</h3>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>git clone https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit.git
cd blazor-toolkit</code></pre>

        <h3>Restore, build, and run the samples</h3>
        <p>From the repository root:</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code># Restore + build the library (matches the CI commands exactly)
dotnet restore src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj
dotnet build  src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj -c Release --no-restore

# Run the interactive samples browser
dotnet run --project samples/Blazor.Toolkit.Samples.Client</code></pre>

        <p>To open the samples in Visual Studio instead, double-click <code>samples/Blazor.Toolkit.Samples.slnx</code> and press F5.</p>

        <h3>Verify your local SDK</h3>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>dotnet --list-sdks</code></pre>
        <p>Make sure one of the listed SDKs matches a <code>&lt;TargetFramework&gt;</code> in the project you are editing. The library targets <code>net8.0</code>, <code>net9.0</code>, and <code>net10.0</code>.</p>

        <div class="cg-callout">
            <strong>CI parity tip:</strong> before opening a PR, run the full solution build with the same properties CI uses:
            <pre class="cg-codeblock" style="margin-top:8px"><code>dotnet build -c Release -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true</code></pre>
            This exercises the same SourceLink, pack, and analyzer rules the PR pipeline runs.
        </div>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="repository-structure" class="cg-toc-anchor">Repository structure</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>A high-level map of the repository. Every path below is relative to the repo root unless otherwise noted.</p>
        <table class="cg-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Path</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>src/</code></td><td>The toolkit library. The main project is <code>Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj</code>; components live under <code>src/Components/&lt;ComponentName&gt;</code> (Buttons, Calendars, Charts, Inputs, Popups, Spinner).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>tests/</code></td><td>Test projects. <code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest</code> is the bUnit unit / component test suite. <code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Playwright.Test</code> contains the Playwright end-to-end test suite (<code>Blazor.Toolkit.playwright.Test/</code>) and the sample app the tests run against (<code>Blazor.Toolkit.Playwright.Samples/</code>).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>samples/</code></td><td>The interactive samples browser that ships as the public documentation site. The Blazor WebAssembly project is <code>samples/Blazor.Toolkit.Samples.Client</code>; the whole browser is in <code>samples/Blazor.Toolkit.Samples.slnx</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>docs/</code></td><td>Public project documents that live alongside the source: <code>docs/API-BREAK-INVENTORY.md</code>, <code>docs/API-COMPATIBILITY.md</code>, and the VPAT accessibility conformance report (<code>docs/VPAT-2.5-INT.md</code>).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>artifacts/</code></td><td>Generated artefacts published from the build pipeline &mdash; currently the SBOM (<code>artifacts/sbom/sbom.cdx.json</code>).</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>.github/</code></td><td>GitHub configuration and maintainer docs: <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code>, <code>DEVELOPMENT.md</code>, <code>CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</code>, <code>PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md</code>, <code>SECURITY.md</code>, <code>SUPPORT.md</code>, <code>TEST-MATRIX.md</code>, <code>THREAT-MODEL.md</code>, the <code>workflows/</code> pipelines, the <code>accessibility/</code> insights, the <code>skills/</code> descriptors, the <code>evidences/</code> archive, and <code>dependabot.yml</code>.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="important-folders" class="cg-toc-anchor">Important folders &amp; resources</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Some folders and resources live outside the obvious <code>src/</code>, <code>tests/</code>, and <code>samples/</code> paths and are easy to miss on a first scan. They are critical to how this project is built, tested, reviewed, and shipped &mdash; please read the ones relevant to your change before opening a PR.</p>

        <h3>Accessibility evidence &mdash; <code>.github/accessibility/</code></h3>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/accessibility" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/accessibility/</code></a> is the home of the per-component accessibility evidence: a rolled-up Accessibility Insights summary and a per-component screen-reader smoke matrix (NVDA, JAWS, Narrator) that is re-verified at every release.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/accessibility/insights-summary.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/accessibility/insights-summary.md</code></a> &mdash; rolled-up Accessibility Insights / FastPass / Assessment results.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/accessibility/screen-reader-smoke.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/accessibility/screen-reader-smoke.md</code></a> &mdash; manual screen-reader smoke matrix per major component.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>For the formal accessibility conformance report, see <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/docs/VPAT-2.5-INT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>docs/VPAT-2.5-INT.md</code></a>.</p>

        <h3>Performance evidence &mdash; <code>.github/evidences/performance/</code></h3>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/evidences/performance" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/evidences/performance/</code></a> captures profiling notes and render-path optimisations that back the perf claims in PRs and release notes.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/evidences/performance/key-usage.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>key-usage.md</code></a> &mdash; key-usage measurements on the major components.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/evidences/performance/render-tree-efficiency.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>render-tree-efficiency.md</code></a> &mdash; render-tree efficiency analysis.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/evidences/performance/shouldRender-optimization.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>shouldRender-optimization.md</code></a> &mdash; <code>ShouldRender</code> optimisation write-up.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/evidences/performance/virtualization-strategy.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>virtualization-strategy.md</code></a> &mdash; virtualisation strategy notes.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Other <code>.github/</code> and root-level resources</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/CONTRIBUTING.md</code></a> &mdash; the canonical version of this guide. The on-site page stays in sync with it.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/DEVELOPMENT.md</code></a> &mdash; build, release, and NuGet sign-and-publish procedure.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md</code></a> &mdash; the PR body template the PR UI pre-fills for you.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/SECURITY.md</code></a> &mdash; the private reporting channel for security issues.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/SUPPORT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/SUPPORT.md</code></a> &mdash; how to get help and where to file issues.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/THREAT-MODEL.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/THREAT-MODEL.md</code></a> &mdash; the threat model that drives the release / signing posture.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/Index.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/Index.md</code></a> &mdash; the index of every document under <code>.github/</code>.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/skills" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/skills/</code></a> &mdash; skill descriptors for AI agents (component-specific: <code>syncfusion-blazor-toolkit-buttons</code>, <code>...-calendars</code>, <code>...-charts</code>, <code>...-inputs</code>, <code>...-notifications</code>, <code>...-popups</code>). Load the matching skill before working on that area.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/workflows" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/workflows/</code></a> &mdash; the CI pipelines: <code>ci.yml</code> (build, test, lint, pack) and <code>codeql.yml</code> (CodeQL security analysis).</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/dependabot.yml" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/dependabot.yml</code></a> &mdash; Dependabot configuration that drives the dependency update PRs.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>CHANGELOG.md</code></a> &mdash; the user-facing changelog. Add an entry under the next unreleased heading if your change is user-visible.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>README.md</code></a> &mdash; top-level project overview, getting-started snippet, and badges.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/Directory.Build.props" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>Directory.Build.props</code></a> &mdash; solution-wide MSBuild properties shared by every project.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/Directory.Build.targets" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>Directory.Build.targets</code></a> &mdash; solution-wide MSBuild targets.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/artifacts/sbom" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>artifacts/sbom/</code></a> &mdash; SBOM artefacts produced by the pipeline (CycloneDX JSON + SHA-256).</li>
        </ul>
    </Content>
