<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="coding-style" class="cg-toc-anchor">Coding style &amp; conventions</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Follow the <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/master/docs/coding-guidelines/coding-style.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">.NET Foundation coding style</a> with <strong>two project-specific exceptions</strong>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>No <code>private</code> keyword.</strong> <code>private</code> is the default accessibility in C#, so we omit it. <code>internal</code>, <code>protected</code>, and <code>public</code> are still written explicitly.</li>
            <li><strong>Hard tabs, not spaces.</strong> The repository is tab-indented; please preserve it.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Other things to keep in mind:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>XML doc comments are required on every public <code>Sf*</code> type and public member. If the docs say a parameter is required, the property must also be marked <code>[EditorRequired]</code>; the <code>EditorRequiredAttributeTests</code> in the bUnit test suite enforces this.</li>
            <li>Match the file layout of neighbouring components: <code>SfFoo.razor</code>, <code>SfFoo.razor.css</code>, <code>SfFoo.razor.cs</code>, <code>Base/SfFooBase.cs</code> if applicable.</li>
            <li>Global JavaScript for the toolkit is shipped from <code>src/wwwroot/scripts/</code>. The SCSS themes that feed into the same assets are built by the <code>blazor-toolkit-themes</code> gulp task (see <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/gulpfile.js" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>gulpfile.js</code></a>). Do not introduce unscoped global identifiers that could collide with the toolkit&rsquo;s public surface.</li>
            <li>Avoid new top-level NuGet dependencies. If you need one, justify it in the PR description.</li>
        </ul>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="making-changes" class="cg-toc-anchor">Making changes &amp; branching strategy</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <ol>
            <li>Fork the repository (or create a branch if you have write access).</li>
            <li>Create a branch from <code>main</code> with a descriptive name. Suggested prefixes: <code>fix/&hellip;</code>, <code>feat/&hellip;</code>, <code>docs/&hellip;</code>, <code>test/&hellip;</code>, <code>chore/&hellip;</code>.</li>
            <li>Make your changes in small, logically grouped commits. Avoid mixing unrelated changes (e.g. a typo fix plus a new feature) in the same PR.</li>
            <li>Build and test locally before pushing.</li>
            <li>Open a pull request targeting <strong><code>main</code></strong>. All PRs target <code>main</code> unless explicitly noted otherwise by a maintainer.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Branches that have been merged are deleted automatically. There is no long-lived release branch; versioning is driven by tags on <code>main</code> (see <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/DEVELOPMENT.md</code></a> for the full release process).</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="writing-tests" class="cg-toc-anchor">Writing tests</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Bug fixes should add a regression test, and new behaviour should add coverage for the happy path and at least one failure case.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Unit / component tests</strong> use <a href="https://bunit.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">bUnit</a> and live in <code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest</code>. The test project mirrors the <code>src/Components/&lt;Name&gt;</code> folder structure.</li>
            <li><strong>End-to-end browser tests</strong> use <a href="https://playwright.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Playwright</a> and live in <code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Playwright.Test/Blazor.Toolkit.playwright.Test</code>. The companion sample app that the specs run against lives in <code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Playwright.Test/Blazor.Toolkit.Playwright.Samples</code>.</li>
            <li>Accessibility evidence (the per-component screen-reader matrix and Accessibility Insights summary) is updated in <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/.github/accessibility" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/accessibility/</code></a>; individual <code>.spec.ts</code> files under <code>Blazor.Toolkit.playwright.Test</code> include axe-core checks as part of the Playwright suite.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Running the bUnit test suite</h3>
        <p>This is the exact command CI runs in the <em>bUnit</em> job:</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>dotnet test tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest/ -c Release \
  --logger "trx;LogFileName=bunit.trx" \
  --results-directory TestResults \
  --collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"</code></pre>

        <h3>Running a single test class</h3>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>dotnet test tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest/ -c Release \
  --no-build --filter "FullyQualifiedName~SfButtonTests"</code></pre>

        <h3>Running the Playwright suite</h3>
        <p>This is the exact command CI runs in the <em>Playwright</em> job:</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>npx playwright test --reporter=line</code></pre>
        <p>The Playwright config (<a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/playwright.config.ts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>playwright.config.ts</code></a>) starts the sample app, runs the specs, and tears the app down &mdash; there is no separate <code>dotnet test</code> step to invoke. To debug a single spec interactively, use <code>npx playwright test --ui</code>.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="submitting-a-pr" class="cg-toc-anchor">Submitting a pull request</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Pull requests are created through the standard GitHub flow. Please read the <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">pull request template</a> in full &mdash; it is short and points out the most common reasons PRs bounce.</p>

        <h3>Checklist before you open the PR</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>The PR targets <code>main</code>.</li>
            <li>All commits reference the issue they fix (e.g. <code>Fixes #1234</code>). The PR body includes <code>Fixes #&hellip;</code> on its own line so GitHub auto-links the issue.</li>
            <li>You have run <code>dotnet build src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj -c Release</code> locally and it succeeds.</li>
            <li>You have added or updated tests, and the bUnit + Playwright suites are green.</li>
            <li><code>Before:</code> / <code>After:</code> screenshots are attached for any visible UI change.</li>
            <li>You have ticked the <strong>&ldquo;Allow edits from maintainers&rdquo;</strong> checkbox. This lets us fix small things and resolve merge conflicts without a round-trip.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>PR title format</h3>
        <p>Use a Conventional Commits style prefix so the changelog stays consistent:</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code>feat(SfButton): add new IconCss parameter
fix(SfDialog): prevent focus loss when closing
docs(contribution): clarify PR review process
test(SfTextBox): cover EditForm validation</code></pre>

        <h3>What happens next</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>CI runs the <em>bUnit</em> matrix (.NET 8 / 9 / 10), <em>Playwright</em>, the <em>NuGet vulnerability scan</em>, <em>ESLint security</em>, the <em>XSS / unsafe markup scan</em>, and a <em>Pack</em> smoke build (unsigned <code>.nupkg</code> per TFM). The unsigned artefact is uploaded for human review only; it is not the published package.</li>
            <li>Two reviewers are assigned automatically. They will respond as quickly as their queue allows.</li>
            <li>If you cannot make the requested changes yourself, say so &mdash; another contributor may pick it up, and you will still be credited.</li>
        </ol>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="review-merge" class="cg-toc-anchor">Review &amp; merge process</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Every pull request is reviewed and tested by at least two members of the Blazor Toolkit team. The team will:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Review for correctness, performance, accessibility, and adherence to the style guide.</li>
            <li>Run the CI pipeline. PRs cannot be merged until CI is green on all three target frameworks.</li>
            <li>Verify the <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PR template</a> sections are complete and the issue is linked.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Once approved and CI is green, a maintainer will squash-merge the PR. The merge commit appears on <code>main</code>, and the changeset is attributed to your GitHub account on the <a href="/contributors">Contributors</a> page.</p>
        <p>NuGet publishing and package signing are <strong>manual</strong> operations performed by the release maintainer; no part of that workflow runs in public CI. See <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/DEVELOPMENT.md</code></a> for the full manual sign-and-publish procedure.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="proposing-larger-features" class="cg-toc-anchor">Proposing larger features / enhancements</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>For anything beyond a small change &mdash; a new component, a new parameter that affects the public API surface, a breaking change &mdash; open an issue first.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Open a <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues/new?assignees=&amp;labels=proposal-open%2C+t%2Fenhancement+%E2%9E%95&amp;template=feature_request.yml&amp;title=%5BEnhancement%5D+YOUR+IDEA!" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Feature Request</a> if you have a problem to solve and want feedback before designing an API.</li>
            <li>Open a <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues/new?assignees=&amp;labels=proposal-open%2C+t%2Fenhancement+%E2%9E%95&amp;template=spec.md&amp;title=[Spec]+" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Spec</a> if you already have a concrete API shape in mind.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Browse the existing issues first &mdash; someone may have already proposed something close, and you can build on their work instead of starting from scratch.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="tips-for-ai-agents" class="cg-toc-anchor">Tips for AI coding agents / automated contributors</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>This section is written for AI agents (Claude, GPT, Gemini, custom agents) so that your contributions match what a human reviewer expects on the first pass.</p>

        <h3>Project facts the agent must know up front</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Repo:</strong> <code>https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit</code> (always operate on the public repo unless the user explicitly says otherwise).</li>
            <li><strong>Base branch:</strong> <code>main</code>. Every PR must target <code>main</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Target frameworks:</strong> <code>net8.0</code>, <code>net9.0</code>, <code>net10.0</code>. The CI matrix builds all three. Code that does not compile on all three is not accepted.</li>
            <li><strong>Style:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/master/docs/coding-guidelines/coding-style.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">.NET Foundation coding style</a> + two project exceptions: <strong>no <code>private</code> keyword</strong>; <strong>hard tabs</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>PR template:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md</code></a> &mdash; include <code>Fixes #&lt;issue&gt;</code> in the body so the issue auto-closes on merge.</li>
            <li><strong>CI gates (defined in <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code></a>):</strong> <em>bUnit</em> (.NET 8 / 9 / 10), <em>Playwright</em> (<code>npx playwright test</code>), <em>NuGet vulnerability scan</em> (<code>dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive</code>), <em>ESLint security</em> (<code>npm run lint:security</code>), <em>XSS / unsafe markup scan</em> (<code>npx gulp security-xss-scan</code>), and <em>Pack</em> (unsigned <code>.nupkg</code> per TFM). PRs must pass every gate on all three target frameworks before merge.</li>
            <li><strong>Allowed secrets:</strong> none in public CI. Do not invent, paste, or reference any GitHub token, NuGet API key, signing key, or environment-specific value in code, comments, or PR descriptions.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Mandatory pre-flight checklist</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Read <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code></a>, <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>DEVELOPMENT.md</code></a>, and the issue you are addressing (or the spec you are implementing).</li>
            <li>Confirm the change is in scope and not blocked by an open discussion. If unsure, open or comment on the issue and stop until a maintainer responds.</li>
            <li>Branch from <code>main</code> with a <code>fix/&hellip;</code> or <code>feat/&hellip;</code> prefix.</li>
            <li>For any non-trivial change, also create a worktree-isolated branch and run the build before writing code, so you have a clean baseline.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Expected commands (copy-paste ready)</h3>
        <p>These are the exact commands the CI pipeline (<a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code></a>) runs. Use the same to reproduce a CI failure locally.</p>
        <pre class="cg-codeblock"><code># 1. Clone and create a branch
git clone https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit.git
cd blazor-toolkit
git checkout -b fix/&lt;short-description&gt; main

# 2. Install npm dependencies (CI runs `npm ci`)
npm ci

# 3. Restore + build (the project, not the slnx, to match CI)
dotnet restore src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj
dotnet build   src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj -c Release --no-restore

# 4. Run the bUnit tests
dotnet test tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest/ -c Release --no-build \
  --logger "trx;LogFileName=bunit.trx"

# 5. Run the Playwright tests (uses the headless config in playwright.config.ts)
npx playwright test --reporter=line

# 6. Run the same security / lint scans CI runs
npm run lint:security
npx gulp security-xss-scan

# 7. Sanity-check the pack step (unsigned .nupkg, like CI)
dotnet pack src/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.csproj -c Release --no-build \
  -o ./unsigned-pkg -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true

# 8. Commit, push, and open the PR targeting main
git add -A
git commit -m "fix(SfButton): describe the change"
git push origin fix/&lt;short-description&gt;
gh pr create --base main --fill</code></pre>

        <h3>Files the agent will most often need to read or edit</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/CONTRIBUTING.md</code></a> &mdash; this document&rsquo;s source of truth.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/DEVELOPMENT.md</code></a> &mdash; build, test, and release procedures.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md</code></a> &mdash; the PR body fields you must fill in.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code></a> &mdash; the CI definition; reproduce failing jobs locally with the commands under <em>Expected commands</em> above.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</code></a> &mdash; the community standards you agree to.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>.github/SECURITY.md</code></a> &mdash; how to report a security issue privately.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/src/Components" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>src/Components/&lt;Name&gt;</code></a> &mdash; the component you are changing. Always read the existing <code>.razor</code>, <code>.razor.cs</code>, and <code>.razor.css</code> in full before editing.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/src/wwwroot/scripts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>src/wwwroot/scripts/</code></a> &mdash; the JavaScript files consumed by the components. Mirror the existing module pattern when adding new scripts.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Toolkit.BUnitTest</code></a> &mdash; mirror the source folder structure when adding bUnit tests.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/tree/main/tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Playwright.Test" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>tests/Syncfusion.Blazor.Playwright.Test</code></a> &mdash; the Playwright test project; the <code>Blazor.Toolkit.playwright.Test/</code> folder holds the specs and the <code>Blazor.Toolkit.Playwright.Samples/</code> folder holds the app the specs run against.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/gulpfile.js" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>gulpfile.js</code></a> &mdash; the gulp tasks referenced by the CI XSS scan (<code>security-xss-scan</code>) and the SCSS theme build (<code>blazor-toolkit-themes</code>).</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Non-negotiable rules for automated contributors</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Never</strong> open a PR that targets a branch other than <code>main</code> unless a maintainer explicitly instructs you to.</li>
            <li><strong>Never</strong> disable, skip, or <code>[Ignore]</code> a CI gate (build warning, analyzer rule, test) to make a build pass. Fix the underlying problem instead.</li>
            <li><strong>Never</strong> invent a public API. If a method or property does not exist, do not pretend it does; either add it to the existing public surface or use what is already there.</li>
            <li><strong>Never</strong> commit generated output, build artefacts, secrets, signing keys, <code>obj/</code>, <code>bin/</code>, <code>node_modules/</code>, or <code>.vs/</code> directories. The repo&rsquo;s <code>.gitignore</code> covers most of them; do not override it.</li>
            <li><strong>Never</strong> widen the public API surface without an issue. <em>Renaming</em>, <em>removing</em>, or <em>changing the signature of</em> a public type or member is a breaking change and is reserved for major versions.</li>
            <li>If the task is ambiguous, prefer the smallest change that resolves the issue and is consistent with existing patterns in the codebase.</li>
        </ul>
    </Content>
</Description>

<Description>
    <Header>
        <h2 id="getting-help" class="cg-toc-anchor">Getting help</h2>
    </Header>
    <Content>
        <p>Stuck? Use whichever channel fits the question.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">GitHub Discussions</a> &mdash; design questions, "how do I&hellip;", proposals before you file an issue.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/issues" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">GitHub Issues</a> &mdash; bug reports, feature requests, spec submissions.</li>
            <li>For security issues, follow the process in <a href="https://github.com/syncfusion/blazor-toolkit/blob/main/.github/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><code>SECURITY.md</code></a> &mdash; do not file a public issue.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Thanks again for helping make the Syncfusion Blazor Toolkit better. Every issue triage, doc fix, and PR helps.</p>
    </Content>
</Description>

